Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test: trace a setup's own machine and post to the posted
 files

The seven rows of #1224, each pinned where its stage lives:
- app setup_mount_trace (new): stored picks, generation with the other
  setup active, the spindle-limit and index-swing verdicts per op's own
  machine, one file per mount in its own dialect (Fanuc / Siemens 840D)
  with its own ops, order and work offset, the document mount moving only
  the following setup, untick and undo, save/reopen byte-identical,
  undo/redo of each pick, the same-mount and half-mount edges.
- app setup_mounts_post: a post that does not serve its own machine. The
  lathe post on a mill setup is refused (#1190); a milling post on a lathe
  setup's turning op posts a milling program - filed as #1232 and kept
  ignored.
- app mcp_setup_mount_trace (new): the machine pick over MCP reaches its
  file and undoes; a setup's own post has no MCP tool (#1233).
- ui setup_mount_pages: the #1206 pin now posts through the shell's Post
  command and asserts each file's dialect and contents.

No product code changed.

Fixes #1224
Refs #1206

